1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,276
On the second of May 2016, a group of footballers

2
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:07,316
sat in a living room in Leicester, watching

3
00:00:07,336 --> 00:00:08,957
someone else's match.

4
00:00:09,207 --> 00:00:12,285
If Tottenham won, the title race went on.

5
00:00:12,385 --> 00:00:15,096
If Tottenham failed to win, Leicester City

6
00:00:15,116 --> 00:00:17,038
were champions of England.

7
00:00:17,388 --> 00:00:20,389
At half-time, Tottenham were winning 2–0.

8
00:00:21,139 --> 00:00:23,745
A year earlier, nobody would have bet on

9
00:00:23,765 --> 00:00:24,565
any of this.

10
00:00:24,585 --> 00:00:27,516
The bookmakers had Leicester at 5000–1.

11
00:00:27,866 --> 00:00:30,892
This is the story of the most unlikely title

12
00:00:30,912 --> 00:00:33,474
in the history of English football.

13
00:00:35,424 --> 00:00:36,288
Chapter one.

14
00:00:36,308 --> 00:00:37,820
The great escape.

15
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,693
To understand how unlikely it was, go back

16
00:00:41,713 --> 00:00:42,964
one more year.

17
00:00:43,114 --> 00:00:45,761
They had come up from the Championship the

18
00:00:45,781 --> 00:00:47,547
year before, as champions.

19
00:00:47,697 --> 00:00:48,867
Christmas 2014.

20
00:00:48,887 --> 00:00:51,723
Leicester City are bottom of the Premier

21
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:52,469
League.

22
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:56,005
In April 2015, they are still bottom, seven

23
00:00:56,025 --> 00:00:57,647
points from safety.

24
00:00:58,097 --> 00:01:01,458
Then, with nine games left, something changes.

25
00:01:01,558 --> 00:01:03,302
They win seven of them.

26
00:01:03,452 --> 00:01:04,528
They finish 14th.

27
00:01:04,548 --> 00:01:07,322
It is one of the great escapes in Premier

28
00:01:07,342 --> 00:01:08,524
League history.

29
00:01:08,974 --> 00:01:11,866
And that summer, the manager who saved them,

30
00:01:11,886 --> 00:01:13,734
Nigel Pearson, is sacked.

31
00:01:15,484 --> 00:01:16,426
Chapter two.

32
00:01:16,446 --> 00:01:17,662
Claudio Ranieri?

33
00:01:17,682 --> 00:01:18,482
Really?

34
00:01:19,432 --> 00:01:22,567
His replacement is a 63-year-old Italian

35
00:01:22,587 --> 00:01:24,660
called Claudio Ranieri.

36
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:27,893
He had managed Chelsea, Valencia, Juventus,

37
00:01:27,913 --> 00:01:29,352
Roma and Inter.

38
00:01:29,452 --> 00:01:32,438
He had never won a top-flight league title.

39
00:01:32,688 --> 00:01:35,501
His last job had ended with Greece losing

40
00:01:35,521 --> 00:01:37,188
to the Faroe Islands.

41
00:01:37,638 --> 00:01:40,229
Gary Lineker, Leicester's most famous former

42
00:01:40,249 --> 00:01:42,844
player, summed up the mood on Twitter.

43
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,189
Claudio Ranieri?

44
00:01:44,209 --> 00:01:45,044
Really?

45
00:01:45,594 --> 00:01:47,127
The bookmakers agreed.

46
00:01:47,147 --> 00:01:50,566
Leicester were 5000–1 to win the league.

47
00:01:50,716 --> 00:01:54,116
Ranieri set his players one target: 40 points,

48
00:01:54,136 --> 00:01:55,153
and safety.

49
00:01:56,903 --> 00:01:57,868
Chapter three.

50
00:01:57,888 --> 00:01:59,062
The bargains.

51
00:02:00,012 --> 00:02:02,909
What Ranieri inherited was a squad of players

52
00:02:02,929 --> 00:02:04,853
other clubs had overlooked.

53
00:02:05,003 --> 00:02:06,643
Kasper Schmeichel in goal.

54
00:02:06,663 --> 00:02:09,355
Wes Morgan and Robert Huth in the middle

55
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:10,344
of defence.

56
00:02:10,794 --> 00:02:13,722
Up front, Jamie Vardy, who had been playing

57
00:02:13,742 --> 00:02:16,174
non-league football until 2012.

58
00:02:16,274 --> 00:02:19,064
Released by Sheffield Wednesday as a teenager,

59
00:02:19,084 --> 00:02:21,715
he had worked in a factory making medical

60
00:02:21,735 --> 00:02:24,685
splints, and played on Saturdays for Stocksbridge

61
00:02:24,705 --> 00:02:25,697
Park Steels.

62
00:02:25,847 --> 00:02:28,292
Leicester signed him from Fleetwood Town

63
00:02:28,312 --> 00:02:30,660
for a reported one million pounds.

64
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:33,657
On the right, Riyad Mahrez, an Algerian

65
00:02:33,677 --> 00:02:36,493
winger from the French second division.

66
00:02:36,593 --> 00:02:40,357
His reported fee: around 400,000 pounds.

67
00:02:40,807 --> 00:02:43,871
And on the third of August 2015, Ranieri

68
00:02:43,891 --> 00:02:45,653
added the last piece.

69
00:02:45,753 --> 00:02:49,182
A midfielder from Caen called N'Golo Kanté,

70
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:52,198
for a reported 5.6 million pounds.

71
00:02:52,348 --> 00:02:55,048
Nobody outside France had heard of him.

72
00:02:55,068 --> 00:02:56,797
By May, everybody had.

73
00:02:57,247 --> 00:02:58,866
Ranieri kept it simple.

74
00:02:58,886 --> 00:03:00,472
Two banks of four.

75
00:03:00,572 --> 00:03:03,535
Win the ball, and give it to Vardy and Mahrez

76
00:03:03,555 --> 00:03:05,106
as fast as possible.

77
00:03:06,856 --> 00:03:07,798
Chapter four.

78
00:03:07,818 --> 00:03:08,902
The record.

79
00:03:09,852 --> 00:03:13,095
Leicester beat Sunderland 4–2 on the opening

80
00:03:13,115 --> 00:03:13,641
day.

81
00:03:13,791 --> 00:03:15,635
They kept coming from behind.

82
00:03:15,655 --> 00:03:18,375
Against Aston Villa in September, they were

83
00:03:18,395 --> 00:03:20,838
2–0 down and won 3–2.

84
00:03:20,988 --> 00:03:23,724
Their only league defeat that autumn was

85
00:03:23,744 --> 00:03:26,940
a heavy one: Arsenal won 5–2 at the King

86
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,612
Power.

87
00:03:27,862 --> 00:03:30,499
And Jamie Vardy started scoring, and did

88
00:03:30,519 --> 00:03:31,391
not stop.

89
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:32,174
One game.

90
00:03:32,194 --> 00:03:33,065
Then another.

91
00:03:33,085 --> 00:03:34,225
Then another.

92
00:03:34,475 --> 00:03:38,246
On the 28th of November 2015, against Manchester

93
00:03:38,266 --> 00:03:41,587
United, he scored in his 11th Premier League

94
00:03:41,607 --> 00:03:43,014
game in a row.

95
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,104
Nobody had ever done that.

96
00:03:45,124 --> 00:03:48,225
The old record of ten belonged to Ruud van

97
00:03:48,245 --> 00:03:49,215
Nistelrooy.

98
00:03:49,765 --> 00:03:52,343
Ranieri had a promise for his defence too.

99
00:03:52,363 --> 00:03:55,148
Keep a clean sheet, and he would buy everyone

100
00:03:55,168 --> 00:03:55,782
pizza.

101
00:03:55,932 --> 00:03:57,709
It took until late October.

102
00:03:57,729 --> 00:04:00,517
When it came, the players had to make the

103
00:04:00,537 --> 00:04:01,910
pizzas themselves.

104
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,617
And when players switched off in training,

105
00:04:04,637 --> 00:04:06,048
he had a catchphrase.

106
00:04:06,098 --> 00:04:07,741
Dilly ding, dilly dong.

107
00:04:07,761 --> 00:04:08,651
Wake up.

108
00:04:10,401 --> 00:04:11,248
Chapter five.

109
00:04:11,268 --> 00:04:12,674
Top at Christmas.

110
00:04:13,624 --> 00:04:16,577
By Christmas 2015, Leicester City were top

111
00:04:16,597 --> 00:04:18,333
of the Premier League.

112
00:04:18,483 --> 00:04:21,408
Twelve months earlier, they had been bottom.

113
00:04:21,958 --> 00:04:24,518
This is usually where stories like this

114
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:25,062
end.

115
00:04:25,162 --> 00:04:28,036
On Boxing Day, they lost 1–0 at Liverpool.

116
00:04:28,056 --> 00:04:31,096
Only their second league defeat of the season.

117
00:04:31,246 --> 00:04:33,651
Everyone waited for the collapse.

118
00:04:35,401 --> 00:04:36,488
Chapter six.

119
00:04:36,508 --> 00:04:37,549
February.

120
00:04:38,499 --> 00:04:40,519
The collapse never came.

121
00:04:40,619 --> 00:04:43,105
On the sixth of February, Leicester went

122
00:04:43,125 --> 00:04:45,451
to Manchester City, the favourites, and

123
00:04:45,471 --> 00:04:46,628
won 3–1.

124
00:04:46,728 --> 00:04:48,325
Robert Huth scored twice.

125
00:04:48,345 --> 00:04:50,157
Mahrez scored the other.

126
00:04:50,607 --> 00:04:53,276
Eight days later, they went to Arsenal.

127
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:56,058
Vardy put them ahead from the penalty spot.

128
00:04:56,078 --> 00:04:58,341
Then Danny Simpson was sent off.

129
00:04:58,491 --> 00:05:00,071
Theo Walcott equalised.

130
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:03,271
And in the 95th minute, Danny Welbeck headed

131
00:05:03,291 --> 00:05:04,071
the winner.

132
00:05:04,091 --> 00:05:05,079
2–1.

133
00:05:05,329 --> 00:05:08,060
It was the last league game Leicester lost

134
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,031
all season.

135
00:05:10,781 --> 00:05:11,991
Chapter seven.

136
00:05:12,011 --> 00:05:12,799
Nerve.

137
00:05:13,749 --> 00:05:15,923
From then on, the pressure was supposed

138
00:05:15,943 --> 00:05:17,004
to break them.

139
00:05:17,104 --> 00:05:19,363
Instead, they ground out results.

140
00:05:19,383 --> 00:05:21,481
A run of 1–0 wins.

141
00:05:21,631 --> 00:05:24,190
On the third of April, Wes Morgan headed

142
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:26,556
the only goal against Southampton.

143
00:05:27,006 --> 00:05:29,761
Against West Ham, Vardy was sent off, and

144
00:05:29,781 --> 00:05:32,420
they needed a stoppage-time penalty from

145
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,944
Leonardo Ulloa to draw 2–2.

146
00:05:35,094 --> 00:05:38,180
Without Vardy, they beat Swansea 4–0.

147
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,507
Only Tottenham were still chasing them.

148
00:05:41,607 --> 00:05:44,149
On the first of May, Leicester drew at Old

149
00:05:44,169 --> 00:05:44,652
Trafford.

150
00:05:44,672 --> 00:05:46,479
One more win would do it.

151
00:05:46,579 --> 00:05:48,483
Or one Tottenham slip.

152
00:05:50,233 --> 00:05:51,212
Chapter eight.

153
00:05:51,232 --> 00:05:52,606
Stamford Bridge.

154
00:05:53,556 --> 00:05:56,309
The next night, Tottenham played at Chelsea.

155
00:05:56,409 --> 00:05:58,713
The Leicester players gathered at Jamie

156
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,297
Vardy's house to watch.

157
00:06:00,547 --> 00:06:03,202
At half-time, Tottenham led 2–0.

158
00:06:03,652 --> 00:06:06,319
In the second half, Gary Cahill scored for

159
00:06:06,339 --> 00:06:07,073
Chelsea.

160
00:06:07,323 --> 00:06:08,818
The game turned ugly.

161
00:06:08,838 --> 00:06:11,695
Tottenham collected nine yellow cards.

162
00:06:11,945 --> 00:06:14,689
Then, late on, Eden Hazard curled in the

163
00:06:14,709 --> 00:06:15,606
equaliser.

164
00:06:15,956 --> 00:06:16,562
2–2.

165
00:06:16,582 --> 00:06:18,709
Tottenham could not catch them.

166
00:06:19,359 --> 00:06:22,848
Leicester City, 5000–1, were champions of

167
00:06:22,868 --> 00:06:23,750
England.

168
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:26,667
Chapter nine.

169
00:06:26,687 --> 00:06:27,793
The trophy.

170
00:06:28,743 --> 00:06:31,336
Five days later, Leicester played Everton

171
00:06:31,356 --> 00:06:32,162
at home.

172
00:06:32,262 --> 00:06:35,036
Andrea Bocelli, a friend of Ranieri's, sang

173
00:06:35,056 --> 00:06:37,110
Nessun Dorma on the pitch.

174
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,692
Vardy scored twice.

175
00:06:38,712 --> 00:06:40,474
Andy King got the other.

176
00:06:40,494 --> 00:06:41,482
3–1.

177
00:06:41,732 --> 00:06:44,559
Then Wes Morgan and Claudio Ranieri lifted

178
00:06:44,579 --> 00:06:46,538
the Premier League trophy.

179
00:06:47,088 --> 00:06:50,108
Leicester finished on 81 points, ten clear

180
00:06:50,128 --> 00:06:51,110
of Arsenal.

181
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,863
They lost three league games all season.

182
00:06:54,313 --> 00:06:57,363
Vardy scored 24 league goals and was named

183
00:06:57,383 --> 00:07:00,649
Footballer of the Year by the football writers.

184
00:07:00,799 --> 00:07:03,695
Mahrez became the first African to win the

185
00:07:03,715 --> 00:07:06,080
PFA Players' Player of the Year.

186
00:07:07,830 --> 00:07:08,728
Chapter ten.

187
00:07:08,748 --> 00:07:10,638
After the fairy tale.

188
00:07:11,588 --> 00:07:14,497
Fairy tales are not supposed to have a second

189
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:14,977
chapter.

190
00:07:14,997 --> 00:07:16,099
This one did.

191
00:07:16,349 --> 00:07:18,640
That summer, Kanté left for Chelsea, and

192
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:21,372
won the league again the following season.

193
00:07:21,522 --> 00:07:23,642
Leicester reached the quarter-finals of

194
00:07:23,662 --> 00:07:25,079
the Champions League.

195
00:07:25,229 --> 00:07:27,514
But in the league they struggled.

196
00:07:27,534 --> 00:07:30,410
In February 2017, nine months after the

197
00:07:30,430 --> 00:07:32,453
trophy, Ranieri was sacked.

198
00:07:33,003 --> 00:07:33,976
Vardy stayed.

199
00:07:33,996 --> 00:07:37,749
In 2020, at 33, he won the Premier League

200
00:07:37,769 --> 00:07:38,946
Golden Boot.

201
00:07:39,396 --> 00:07:42,517
In October 2018, the club's owner, Vichai

202
00:07:42,537 --> 00:07:45,593
Srivaddhanaprabha, died when his helicopter

203
00:07:45,613 --> 00:07:49,004
crashed outside the stadium after a match.

204
00:07:49,554 --> 00:07:52,630
In 2021, Leicester won the FA Cup for the

205
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:54,828
first time in their history.

206
00:07:55,578 --> 00:07:58,201
Every season since, someone asks the same

207
00:07:58,221 --> 00:07:58,751
question.

208
00:07:58,771 --> 00:08:00,453
Could it happen again?

209
00:08:00,703 --> 00:08:03,029
The money in football has only grown.

210
00:08:03,049 --> 00:08:05,961
The gap between the richest clubs and everyone

211
00:08:05,981 --> 00:08:07,777
else is wider than ever.

212
00:08:08,127 --> 00:08:12,302
Which is what makes 2015–16 so hard to believe.

213
00:08:12,452 --> 00:08:14,669
A manager nobody wanted.

214
00:08:14,689 --> 00:08:16,586
Players nobody rated.

215
00:08:16,606 --> 00:08:17,814
5000–1.

216
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:19,420
It happened once.

217
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:22,060
Will we ever see another Leicester?

218
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,681
Tell us in the comments.

219
00:08:24,131 --> 00:08:26,325
You're watching Offside Stories.

220
00:08:26,345 --> 00:08:28,182
Beyond the 90 minutes.
